# There was no .dockerignore here at all, so every `docker build ./frontend`
# (compose builds the frontend from this directory) uploaded ~984 MB and then
# `COPY . .` baked it into the image.
#
# Measured 2026-09-20: context is now 17.5 MB in 102 files, nearly all of it
# public/ images. If it climbs back over ~50 MB, something below stopped
# matching and node_modules or .next is being shipped again.

# 663 MB, and worse than just big: these are darwin-arm64 native binaries from a
# developer's Mac being copied into a linux/amd64 image, where the sharp and
# canvas bindings do not load. The Dockerfile runs its own install; the host
# copy can only shadow it.
node_modules

# 304 MB of a build produced on the host. `npm run build` regenerates it, and a
# stale .next copied in first has served old pages mid-class.
.next
out
*.tsbuildinfo

# SECRETS. .env.local holds the real API and Keycloak URLs and was being copied
# into the image, where it also beats the runtime environment: Next.js loads
# .env.local over the values compose passes in, so a baked file silently points
# a production container at a developer's localhost.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Not build input.
.git
.gitignore
Dockerfile
Dockerfile.*
.dockerignore
*.md
.DS_Store
*.log
npm-debug.log*
coverage
